# Engine / dictionary

- Pure TypeScript — no React/DOM.
- Vitest for path rules, scoring, board gen (incl. gen-within-retry-cap on seeded RNG), dict filters, **minWordLength** (short reject + achievable targets), letter-variety weighting.
- Single authoritative thresholds/scoring config object; loosen there if gen flakes — never ad-hoc in UI.
- **Goal `TARGET_RATIOS` + `TARGET_CAPS`** (`config.ts`): Easy **0.25** / Med **0.40** / Hard **0.65** of `maxScore`, then absolute caps Easy **36** / Med **75** / Hard **105** via `computeTargets`. Tune only there — points not word count; caps stop dense crumb boards from showing unbounded “points left”. Keep Easy < Med < Hard and Hard under board-clear; `HARD_TARGET_FLOOR` still lifts Hard on lean boards (clamped to maxScore). Don’t raise `scoreWord` just to soften Goal — that rebalances Timed / Survival / medals.
- `minWordLength` on `GameConfig`: maxScore/targets/allWords/missed filter to ≥ N; targets always ≤ maxScore.
- **No max word length** — `findAllWords` / `submitPath` only require path + dictionary + min floor. Gen `ge5`/`ge6`/`ge7`/`ge8`/`ge10` are “≥ N words” quality floors, never a length ceiling (10+ allowed whenever a path exists). Max path length = grid cells (N²). Larger grids raise mid/long floors in `BOARD_THRESHOLDS` (soft `ge10: 1` on square 5×5 / 6×6 and hex 6×6) while `ge3`/`total` keep short crumbs; every entry keeps `ge6 ≥ 1`; scaled retries keep that floor (≥1 never loosens to 0); soft ge7+/ge10 may scale to 0; fallback quality ranks by long-word density (heavy weight on 8+/10+) when full thresholds can’t clear. `GEN_RETRY_CAP` **100**.
- Dictionary: enable1 + popular + NSFW blocklist + given-name filter → build artifact; **play = popular** (`popular.json`); full ENABLE kept for a future dictionary mode.
- **Play lexicon:** `dict.has` / board `allWords` / targets / Words left = **popular − NSFW − given names**. Never gate play on full ENABLE (obscure Scrabble scraps). `isPopular` matches `has` in v1; Results Long ones left still filters with `isPopular` + length floor.
- **Board letter mix by difficulty:** `generateBoard({ difficulty })` → `randomBoard` picks each tile from `letterMixWeights(placedCounts, difficulty)` (`config.ts`), which flattens `LETTER_WEIGHTS` per `LETTER_VARIETY[difficulty]`, applies Easy `vowelBoost`, and docks letters already placed this board. Easy ≈ common bias + vowel lean + light anti-repeat (crumb-friendly); Hard flattens hardest + docks repeats hardest. Easy also uses `thresholdsForDifficulty` (softer ge5+/ge7+ floors; `ge6 ≥ 1` kept) and ranks fallback boards by short-word density instead of 8+/10+. `difficulty` defaults to `"medium"` (timed has none). Tune only `LETTER_VARIETY` + Easy threshold scaling — verify with the real dict (`createDictionary()`) that thresholds still clear before loosening further.
- **Survival mode** (`GameConfig.mode: "survival"`, `config.ts` + `game.ts`): shares `GameState.remainingMs`/`tickTimer` with timed (same "ends `timeout` at 0" path) but refills on every accepted word instead of counting a fixed sprint down. `createGame` seeds `remainingMs` from `SURVIVAL_START_SECONDS[difficulty]`; `submitPath` adds `survivalBonusSeconds(points, difficulty)` (seconds) onto `remainingMs` and returns it as `SubmitResult.bonusSeconds` for UI feedback. Tune starting time / refill rate / difficulty multiplier only in those `config.ts` constants — never re-derive bonus math in the UI. Board gen is unchanged (pass `difficulty` through like target mode; survival has no points target so `board.targets` is unused).
